# Run artifacts for the walker2d_lut chapter — regenerable, kept out of git.
# (The repo-wide rule only covers experiments/**/*.pt; SB3 writes .zip and the JAX
#  side writes .msgpack, so they are named explicitly here.)
#
# NOTE: patterns are deliberately UNANCHORED (no leading path segment). A pattern
# containing a mid-string "/" is anchored to this directory, so "run_seed*/ckpt/"
# would NOT match exp_c01_sac_baseline/run_seed0/ckpt/ — use "**/" or a bare glob.

# Checkpoints / trained weights
**/ckpt/
*.zip
*.msgpack

# Raw frame dumps, video, and debug contact sheets (figures ARE committed)
*.npz
*.mp4
cam_*.png

# TensorBoard event files
**/tb/

# Full per-iteration PPO log (482 KB of JSON); the downsampled curve is committed
ppo_mjx_full.json
ppo_mjx_108.json
*.json.partial

# Local scratch
__pycache__/
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
.slack_*.handle

# exp_c03/c04/c05 artifacts
obs.npy
act.npy
*.npy
torch_reference.npz
sweep_partial.json

# exp_c06
torch_grads.npz
lut_scratch_params.npz
ppo_lut_scratch.json

# in-progress artifacts
*.partial

# Deliberate exception: the four completed 2x2 actor checkpoints (114 KB each,
# 456 KB total). They are the deliverable artifacts of a finished study and are
# what any re-evaluation needs without a 30-minute retrain. Everything else stays
# out -- this is a narrow negation, not a relaxation of the no-checkpoints rule.
!exp_c09_lut_sac/lut_sac_c11_*_actor.npz

# Second deliberate exception: the single best LUT-SAC policy of the chapter
# (exp_c21, seed 4 @ 20,000 iters, hyperplane x hard, CPU-reference 5647.5 --
# the first from-scratch LUT past all three anchors). 114 KB. This is the one
# deployable artifact worth carrying in git; its @10k sibling, the snapshot
# trace, and every other c12-c22 actor stay out.
!exp_c09_lut_sac/lut_sac_c21_seed4_20k_actor.npz

# ...and its 4-bit quantized twin (32 KB): int4 symmetric per-table codes for both
# the table content and the addressing, CPU-reference 5743.1 = 101.7% of the fp32
# policy. make_int4.py regenerates it from the actor above, so this negation buys
# convenience rather than irreplaceability -- but it is the deployable artifact.
!exp_c09_lut_sac/lut_sac_c21_seed4_20k_int4.npz
